<section class="mira-card" aria-labelledby="mira-info-title">
  <div class="mira-card-head">
    <span class="mira-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2l1.7 5.3L19 9l-5.3 1.7L12 16l-1.7-5.3L5 9l5.3-1.7L12 2z"/><path d="M19 15l.8 2.4L22 18l-2.2.6L19 21l-.8-2.4L16 18l2.2-.6L19 15z"/></svg>
    </span>
    <h2 id="mira-info-title">What Mira is</h2>
  </div>
  <p>
    Mira is your school's built-in AI assistant — an educational intelligence that understands how
    your workspace runs. Ask it a question, hand it a task, or have it pull together a summary, and
    it works directly inside the app on your behalf: looking up students, guardians, fees, attendance,
    classes, and assessments, drafting messages, and carrying out real actions across the app through
    a simple conversation.
  </p>
  <ul class="mira-point-list">
    <li><span class="mira-point-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span> Built for easy management — Mira turns multi-step, click-through tasks into a single request.</li>
    <li><span class="mira-point-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span> Scoped strictly to your own school — Mira never sees or touches another school's data.</li>
    <li><span class="mira-point-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span> Permission-aware by design — Mira only ever does what the real permissions granted below already allow, nothing more.</li>
    <li><span class="mira-point-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span> Fully auditable — every change Mira makes is recorded in Activity Logs, tagged "via Mira (AI assistant)".</li>
    <li><span class="mira-point-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span> Runs as its own dedicated service and opens in its own tab, alongside the rest of the app.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
